@node Introduction
@chapter Introduction

@cindex introduction
@cindex overview

List Manager is an Emacs package that provides a comprehensive set of
functions for managing lists in org-mode and LaTeX documents.  It
simplifies common list manipulation tasks such as converting between
different list formats, extracting unchecked items from checklists,
and recovering LaTeX formatting that has been stripped by external tools.

@section Features

List Manager provides the following key features:

@itemize @bullet
@item
Convert numbered, dash, asterisk, and plus lists to LaTeX @code{\item} format.

@item
Extract and cut unchecked items from org-mode and LaTeX checklists.

@item
Convert between org-mode checklists and regular lists.

@item
Convert unordered lists to ordered (numbered) lists.

@item
Wrap list items in complete LaTeX environments (@code{itemize}, @code{enumerate}).

@item
Recover LaTeX formatting stripped by tools like 750words.

@item
Split paragraphs into individual sentences.

@item
Add periods to list items missing terminal punctuation.
@end itemize

@section Supported List Formats

List Manager supports the following list formats:

@table @samp
@item Org-mode dash lists
Lines beginning with @code{- item text}.

@item Org-mode asterisk lists
Lines beginning with @code{* item text}.

@item Org-mode plus lists
Lines beginning with @code{+ item text}.

@item Org-mode numbered lists
Lines beginning with @code{1. item text}.

@item Org-mode checklists
Lines with @code{- [ ] item} (unchecked) or @code{- [X] item} (checked).

@item LaTeX item lists
Lines with @code{\item item text}.

@item LaTeX checklists
Lines with @code{\item [ ] item} or @code{\item[\checked] item}.
@end table

@node Installation
@chapter Installation

@cindex installation
@cindex setup

List Manager requires GNU Emacs 26.1 or later.  The dependencies
@code{org} and @code{cl-lib} both ship with Emacs.

@section Manual Installation

List Manager is not yet on MELPA.  To install manually, clone the
repository and add it to your load path:

@example
git clone https://github.com/MooersLab/list-manager.git
@end example

Then add to your init file:

@lisp
(add-to-list 'load-path "/path/to/list-manager")
(require 'list-manager)
@end lisp

@section Installing with use-package

@lisp
(use-package list-manager
  :load-path "/path/to/list-manager")
@end lisp

@section Installing the Info Manual

To install the Info manual for access via @kbd{C-h i} without root
access:

@example
cd /path/to/list-manager
make info
make install-info-user
@end example

Then add the directory to your init file:

@lisp
(add-to-list 'Info-directory-list "~/.local/share/info")
@end lisp

Alternatively, build and install by hand:

@example
makeinfo list-manager.texi
sudo install-info --info-dir=/usr/share/info list-manager.info
@end example

@node Quick Start
@chapter Quick Start

@cindex quick start
@cindex tutorial

This chapter provides a quick introduction to using List Manager.

@section Basic Workflow

@enumerate
@item
Select a region containing a list.

@item
Call the appropriate conversion function using the key binding or @kbd{M-x}.

@item
The region is replaced with the converted list.
@end enumerate

@section Example: Converting a Dash List to LaTeX

Suppose you have the following org-mode list:

@example
- First item
- Second item
- Third item
@end example

Select the region and press @kbd{C-c x d} (or @kbd{M-x list-manager-dash-list-to-latex-items}).
The list becomes:

@example
\item First item
\item Second item
\item Third item
@end example

@section Example: Extracting Unchecked Items

Given a checklist:

@example
- [ ] Buy groceries
- [X] Call doctor
- [ ] Write report
- [X] Send email
@end example

Select the region and press @kbd{C-c x u} (or @kbd{M-x list-manager-extract-unchecked-items}).
A new buffer @file{*Unchecked Items*} opens containing:

@example
- [ ] Buy groceries
- [ ] Write report
@end example

@node Converting Lists
@chapter Converting Lists

@cindex converting lists
@cindex list conversion

This chapter describes functions for converting between different list formats.

@section Numbered Lists to LaTeX

@deffn Command list-manager-numbered-list-to-latex-items
@findex list-manager-numbered-list-to-latex-items
Convert a numbered list to LaTeX @code{\item} statements.

Input:
@example
1. First item
2. Second item
3. Third item
@end example

Output:
@example
\item First item
\item Second item
\item Third item
@end example
@end deffn

@section Dash Lists to LaTeX

@deffn Command list-manager-dash-list-to-latex-items
@findex list-manager-dash-list-to-latex-items
Convert a dash, asterisk, or plus list to LaTeX @code{\item} statements.
Works with @code{-}, @code{*}, and @code{+} markers.
@end deffn

@deffn Command list-manager-org-dash-list-to-latex-items
@findex list-manager-org-dash-list-to-latex-items
Convert an org-mode dash list to LaTeX @code{\item} format with proper
indentation.  Works on the selected region or the entire buffer.
@end deffn

@section Creating Complete LaTeX Environments

@deffn Command list-manager-org-dash-list-to-latex-itemize
@findex list-manager-org-dash-list-to-latex-itemize
Convert an org-mode dash list to a complete LaTeX @code{itemize}
environment, wrapped in org-mode export blocks.

Input:
@example
- First item
- Second item
@end example

Output:
@example
#+BEGIN_EXPORT latex
\begin@{itemize@}
    \item First item
    \item Second item
\end@{itemize@}
#+END_EXPORT
@end example
@end deffn

@deffn Command list-manager-org-dash-list-to-custom-latex
@findex list-manager-org-dash-list-to-custom-latex
Convert an org-mode dash list to a custom LaTeX format suitable for
Beamer slideshows, with @code{\Large} font and custom bullet formatting.
@end deffn

@section Converting Lines to Lists

@deffn Command list-manager-lines-to-latex-items start end &optional arg
@findex list-manager-lines-to-latex-items
Convert each line in the region to a LaTeX @code{\item}.  Empty lines
are skipped.  With prefix argument @var{arg} (@kbd{C-u}), wrap the items
in an @code{itemize} environment.
@end deffn

@deffn Command list-manager-lines-in-region-to-org-list marker
@findex list-manager-lines-in-region-to-org-list
Convert lines in the region to an org-mode list with the specified
@var{marker} (@code{-}, @code{+}, or @code{*}).  Prompts for the marker
interactively.
@end deffn

@section Unordered to Ordered Lists

@deffn Command list-manager-org-convert-unordered-to-ordered-list start end
@findex list-manager-org-convert-unordered-to-ordered-list
Convert unnumbered list items (using @code{-}, @code{+}, or @code{*})
to numbered list items in the marked region.

Input:
@example
- First item
- Second item
- Third item
@end example

Output:
@example
1. First item
2. Second item
3. Third item
@end example
@end deffn

@node Checklist Operations
@chapter Checklist Operations

@cindex checklists
@cindex unchecked items
@cindex todo items

This chapter describes functions for working with checklists.

@section Extracting Unchecked Items

@deffn Command list-manager-extract-unchecked-items start end
@findex list-manager-extract-unchecked-items
Extract unchecked checklist items from the region and display them in
a new buffer named @file{*Unchecked Items*}.  Supports multiple formats:

@itemize @bullet
@item
Org-mode style: @code{- [ ] item} vs @code{- [X] item}

@item
LaTeX style 1: @code{\item [ ] item} vs @code{\item [X] item}

@item
LaTeX style 2: @code{\item item} vs @code{\item[\checked] item}
@end itemize
@end deffn

@deffn Command list-manager-extract-unchecked-items-to-kill-ring start end
@findex list-manager-extract-unchecked-items-to-kill-ring
Like @code{list-manager-extract-unchecked-items}, but copies the
unchecked items to the kill ring instead of a new buffer.  Useful for
pasting items elsewhere.
@end deffn

@section Cutting Unchecked Items

@deffn Command list-manager-cut-unchecked-items start end
@findex list-manager-cut-unchecked-items
Cut (remove) unchecked items from the region and display them in a new
buffer.  The original buffer retains only the checked items.
@end deffn

@deffn Command list-manager-cut-unchecked-items-to-kill-ring start end
@findex list-manager-cut-unchecked-items-to-kill-ring
Cut unchecked items and place them in the kill ring instead of a new buffer.
@end deffn

@section Converting Checklists

@deffn Command list-manager-convert-org-checklist-to-dash-list begin end
@findex list-manager-convert-org-checklist-to-dash-list
Convert org-mode checklist items to simple dash list items.  Removes
the checkbox markers @code{[ ]} or @code{[X]} while preserving indentation.

Input:
@example
- [ ] Unchecked item
- [X] Checked item
@end example

Output:
@example
- Unchecked item
- Checked item
@end example
@end deffn

@deffn Command list-manager-org-convert-list-in-region-to-checkboxes start end
@findex list-manager-org-convert-list-in-region-to-checkboxes
Convert a dash/hyphen bullet list to org-mode checkboxes.

Input:
@example
- Item one
- Item two
@end example

Output:
@example
- [ ] Item one
- [ ] Item two
@end example
@end deffn

@deffn Command list-manager-org-convert-checkboxes-in-region-to-list start end
@findex list-manager-org-convert-checkboxes-in-region-to-list
Convert org-mode checkboxes back to a regular dash list, removing
checkbox markers.
@end deffn

@section Carrying Forward Todos

@deffn Command list-manager-carry-forward-todos
@findex list-manager-carry-forward-todos
Carry forward undone TODOs and unchecked items to a ``Next Week''
heading while preserving category organization.  Useful for weekly
planning in org-mode.  The function:

@enumerate
@item
Collects undone TODOs and unchecked items from the current heading.

@item
Creates or finds a ``Next Week'' heading.

@item
Inserts items under their respective categories.

@item
Marks original items as done.
@end enumerate
@end deffn

@section Converting Lines and Strings to Checklists

@deffn Command list-manager-org-convert-lines-to-org-checklist beg end
@findex list-manager-org-convert-lines-to-org-checklist
Convert the lines in the region to org-mode checklist items.  Existing
checkboxes, indentation, and empty lines are preserved.  When no region
is active, the whole buffer is used.
@end deffn

@deffn Function list-manager-string-to-org-checklist text
@findex list-manager-string-to-org-checklist
Return @var{text} converted to org-mode checklist format.  This is a
non-interactive helper used by other commands.
@end deffn

@deffn Command list-manager-org-checklist-from-kill-ring
@findex list-manager-org-checklist-from-kill-ring
Convert the most recent kill-ring entry to an org checklist and place
the result back on the kill ring.
@end deffn

@node Format Conversions
@chapter Format Conversions

@cindex format conversions
@cindex todo headlines
@cindex latex to org

This chapter describes the commands that convert among LaTeX items, org
dash lists, org checklists, and org TODO headlines.  Each command acts on
the active region.

@section LaTeX Items to Org

@deffn Command list-manager-convert-latex-items-to-dash-list begin end
@findex list-manager-convert-latex-items-to-dash-list
Convert LaTeX @code{\item} entries to org-mode dash list items,
preserving indentation.
@end deffn

@deffn Command list-manager-convert-latex-items-to-org-checklist begin end
@findex list-manager-convert-latex-items-to-org-checklist
Convert LaTeX @code{\item} entries to unchecked org-mode checklist items.
@end deffn

@deffn Command list-manager-convert-latex-items-to-todo-headlines begin end
@findex list-manager-convert-latex-items-to-todo-headlines
Convert LaTeX @code{\item} entries to level-one @code{TODO} headlines.
@end deffn

@section Org Checklists and Dash Lists to LaTeX

@deffn Command list-manager-convert-org-checklist-to-latex-items begin end
@findex list-manager-convert-org-checklist-to-latex-items
Convert org-mode checklist items, whether checked or unchecked, to LaTeX
@code{\item} entries.  The checkbox markup is removed.
@end deffn

@section Dash Lists and Checklists to TODO Headlines

@deffn Command list-manager-convert-dash-list-to-todo-headlines begin end
@findex list-manager-convert-dash-list-to-todo-headlines
Convert org-mode dash list items to level-one @code{TODO} headlines.
@end deffn

@deffn Command list-manager-convert-checklist-to-todo-headlines begin end
@findex list-manager-convert-checklist-to-todo-headlines
Convert org-mode checklist items to headlines.  Unchecked items become
@code{TODO} headlines and checked items become @code{DONE} headlines.
@end deffn

@section TODO Headlines to Lists

@deffn Command list-manager-convert-todo-headlines-to-dash-list begin end
@findex list-manager-convert-todo-headlines-to-dash-list
Convert org-mode @code{TODO}, @code{DONE}, and related headlines to dash
list items, removing the keyword and the leading stars.
@end deffn

@deffn Command list-manager-convert-todo-headlines-to-checklist begin end
@findex list-manager-convert-todo-headlines-to-checklist
Convert org-mode headlines to checklist items.  @code{DONE} and
@code{CANCELLED} headlines become checked items; @code{TODO},
@code{WAITING}, @code{NEXT}, and @code{SOMEDAY} headlines become
unchecked items.
@end deffn

@deffn Command list-manager-convert-todo-headlines-to-latex-items begin end
@findex list-manager-convert-todo-headlines-to-latex-items
Convert org-mode @code{TODO} and @code{DONE} headlines to LaTeX
@code{\item} entries, removing the keyword and the leading stars.
@end deffn

@section Region to Org Itemized List

@deffn Command list-manager-org-region-to-itemized-list
@findex list-manager-org-region-to-itemized-list
Convert every line in the selected region to an org-mode dash list item.
@end deffn

@node LaTeX Operations
@chapter LaTeX Operations

@cindex LaTeX
@cindex itemize
@cindex enumerate

This chapter describes LaTeX-specific list operations.

@section Region to Itemized List

@deffn Command list-manager-latex-region-to-itemized-list start end
@findex list-manager-latex-region-to-itemized-list
Convert the region to a complete LaTeX @code{itemize} environment.
Each line becomes an @code{\item}.  Empty lines produce empty items.

Input:
@example
First item
Second item
Third item
@end example

Output:
@example
\begin@{itemize@}
\item First item
\item Second item
\item Third item
\end@{itemize@}
@end example
@end deffn

@section CSV to Itemized List

@deffn Command list-manager-latex-convert-csv-to-itemized-list start end
@findex list-manager-latex-convert-csv-to-itemized-list
Convert a comma-separated list to a LaTeX @code{itemize} environment.

Input:
@example
apple, banana, cherry
@end example

Output:
@example
\begin@{itemize@}
  \item apple
  \item banana
  \item cherry
\end@{itemize@}
@end example
@end deffn

@section Unchecked LaTeX Items

@deffn Command list-manager-lines-to-latex-items-unchecked start end &optional arg
@findex list-manager-lines-to-latex-items-unchecked
Convert each line in the region to a LaTeX @code{\item} for use with
the @code{\checked}/@code{\unchecked} system.  With prefix argument
@var{arg}, wrap in an @code{itemize} environment with
@code{label=\unchecked}.
@end deffn

@node 750words Recovery
@chapter 750words Recovery

@cindex 750words
@cindex formatting recovery

The website 750words.com is useful for daily writing practice but
strips LaTeX formatting.  List Manager provides functions to recover
this formatting.

@section Adding Backslashes

@deffn Command list-manager-add-backslashes &optional start end
@findex list-manager-add-backslashes
Add backslashes in front of LaTeX keywords that 750words strips.
Operates on the active region or the entire buffer.

Keywords restored: @code{chapter}, @code{section}, @code{subsection},
@code{subsubsection}, @code{include}, @code{begin}, @code{end},
@code{index}, @code{label}, and @code{item}.

Before:
@example
section@{Introduction@}
begin@{itemize@}
item First
end@{itemize@}
@end example

After:
@example
\section@{Introduction@}
\begin@{itemize@}
\item First
\end@{itemize@}
@end example
@end deffn

@section Restoring Newlines

@deffn Command list-manager-restore-newlines &optional start end
@findex list-manager-restore-newlines
Restore newlines before LaTeX list keywords that 750words strips.
Inserts a newline before @code{\item}, @code{\begin}, and @code{\end}
when they are not already at the beginning of a line.
@end deffn

@section Combined Recovery

@deffn Command list-manager-restore-latex-formatting &optional start end
@findex list-manager-restore-latex-formatting
Restore both backslashes and newlines stripped by 750words.  Runs
@code{list-manager-add-backslashes} followed by
@code{list-manager-restore-newlines}.
@end deffn

@section Repairing Flattened Item Lists

@deffn Command list-manager-repair-stripped-item-list beg end
@findex list-manager-repair-stripped-item-list
Rebuild a LaTeX @code{\item} list that was flattened into a single line
with the backslashes removed.  A bare word @code{item} is restored to
@code{\item} and placed on its own line only when it stands as a whole
word, so the command is safe to run twice and never splits words such as
@code{itemize}.

Before:
@example
item Do this. item Do that.
@end example

After:
@example
\item Do this.
\item Do that.
@end example
@end deffn

@node Text Manipulation
@chapter Text Manipulation

@cindex text manipulation
@cindex sentences
@cindex blank lines

This chapter describes text manipulation utilities.

@section Splitting by Sentences

@deffn Command list-manager-split-line-by-sentences start end
@findex list-manager-split-line-by-sentences
Move each sentence in the region to its own line.  Ignores common
titles and abbreviations such as Dr., Mr., Mrs., Ph.D., and M.S.
Useful for working with transcripts from speech-to-text tools like Whisper.

Before:
@example
Dr. Smith said hello. Mr. Jones agreed. It was a good day.
@end example

After:
@example
Dr. Smith said hello.
Mr. Jones agreed.
It was a good day.
@end example
@end deffn

@section Removing Blank Lines

@deffn Command list-manager-remove-blank-lines-in-region start end
@findex list-manager-remove-blank-lines-in-region
Remove all blank lines in the region.  Blank lines include empty lines
and lines containing only whitespace.
@end deffn

@section Adding Periods to List Items

@deffn Command list-manager-org-or-latex-add-periods-to-list
@findex list-manager-org-or-latex-add-periods-to-list
Add a period to the end of each line in the current list if missing.
Works with org-mode lists, org-mode checklists, and LaTeX @code{\item}
lists.  Place the cursor anywhere in the list and invoke this command.
@end deffn

@deffn Command list-manager-org-add-periods-to-list-items begin end
@findex list-manager-org-add-periods-to-list-items
Add a period to each item of the selected org-mode list if missing.
Both checked and unchecked checkboxes and the leading dash are preserved.
@end deffn

@section Reflowing to One Sentence Per Line

@deffn Command list-manager-unwrap-to-one-sentence-per-line &optional beg end
@findex list-manager-unwrap-to-one-sentence-per-line
Reflow the region, or the current paragraph, to one sentence per line.
First the wrapped lines of the paragraph are joined, then a newline is
inserted after each sentence so that every sentence sits on its own line.
@end deffn

